</DL>

<A NAME=S8></A>
<H2>Summary</H2>
<UL>
<LI>A file type is a number; <CODE>File$Type_xxx</CODE> names it, <CODE>Alias$@RunType_xxx</CODE> says what
double-clicking runs, and the <CODE>file_xxx</CODE> sprite is its icon. <CODE>!Boot</CODE> sets them.<P>
<LI>In an Obey file <CODE>%0</CODE>-<CODE>%9</CODE> and <CODE>%*0</CODE> are its parameters; <CODE>%%</CODE>
is a <CODE>%</CODE>.<P>
<LI>A <CODE>toJSON</CODE> method decides what <CODE>JSON.stringify</CODE> saves; a <CODE>static</CODE> method
belongs to the class. Put a format name and a version number in every file you design.<P>
<LI>A <CODE>Document</CODE> class keeps one open file's data, name, modified flag and window together.<P>
<LI>Show the file's name and a <CODE>*</CODE> while it is changed; save with F3 and the Save box; ask
Discard/Cancel/Save before closing a changed document.<P>
<LI>A file passed to a program arrives in <CODE>ctx.argv[0]</CODE>. The Filer offers a double-clicked file
to running tasks with <CODE>DataOpen</CODE> first; claim it to open it in the running copy.<P>
</UL>

<A NAME=S9></A>
<H2>Exercises</H2>
<DL>
<DT><DD>1  Put the number of contacts in the title, after the file's name: <CODE>Friends (10)</CODE>.<P>
<DT><DD>2  Add an item <I>New book</I> to the icon bar menu, doing what Select on the icon does.<P>
<DT><DD>3  <CODE>fromJSON</CODE> accepts any version. Make it refuse files whose version is greater than 1,
with the message <I>This file was made by a newer Contacts</I>.<P>
<DT><DD>4  Quitting from the icon bar menu asks once about all the changed books. Change it so that it goes
through them, closing each one with its own Discard/Cancel/Save box, and quits only if they all close.<P>
</DL>

<A NAME=S10></A>
<H2>Answers</H2>
<DL>
<DT><DD>1  The title is made in one place, the getter:
<PRE>
get title() {
  const name = this.filename || '&lt;untitled&gt;';
  const full = `${name} (${this.book.size})`;
  return this.modified ? full + ' *' : full;
}
</PRE>
It changes whenever a contact is added or removed, because every change calls <CODE>setModified</CODE>.<P>
<DT><DD>2  Add <CODE>{ text: 'New book', action: () =&gt; new Document(app) }</CODE> before Quit in
<CODE>menu</CODE>.<P>
<DT><DD>3  In <CODE>fromJSON</CODE>, after the format check:
<PRE>
if (data.version &gt; 1) {
  throw new Error('This file was made by a newer Contacts');
}
</PRE>
<DT><DD>4  <CODE>close</CODE> resolves <CODE>true</CODE> if the document closed:
<PRE>
const quit = async () =&gt; {
  for (const d of [...app.docs]) {
    if (!(await d.close())) return;
  }
  task.quit();
};
</PRE>
(<CODE>[...app.docs]</CODE> makes a copy, because closing a document takes it out of the set.) A document
whose Save box is still open counts as not closed, so Contacts doesn't quit under it.<P>
</DL>

